    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="1090" n="980" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg980"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">367.1164 Brusa School Trial/56</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 12.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 545</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the Embassy’s
                    despatch No. 520 of October 2, 1928,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d816-f1"/> and with
                    further reference to the reopening of the Brusa school to inform the Department
                    that, according to a letter dated October 20, 1928, a copy of which is enclosed,
                    from Mr. Luther R. Fowle, <pb facs="1091" n="981" xml:id="pg981"/> Treasurer of
                    the Turkey Mission of the American Board,<anchor n="67" xml:id="d816-f2"/> the
                    petition of Miss Jillson to reopen the American School at Brusa has been refused
                    by the Ministry of Public Instruction.</p>
                <p>Mr. Fowle, in referring to the enclosed copy of a communication from the Director
                    of Education at Brusa, dated October 14, 1928,<anchor n="67" xml:id="d816-f3"/>
                    is of the opinion that if perchance the case should finally end in an acquittal
                    of Miss Jillson the position taken by the Minister of Public Instruction “would
                    logically seem to make necessary the reopening of the School”.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Chargé d’Affaires at interim:<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Ernest L. Ives</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">First Secretary of Embassy</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
